WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.080
Network kindly, prove your work, and plan your next 90 days.

2
00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:09.150
This is the video for module four of Personal Branding and Online Presence.

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:22.200
Networking online follows the same rules as networking at a wedding. Introduce yourself politely, show interest in the other person, offer value before you ask for anything, and follow up.

4
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.670
Connect with peers, who can share knowledge and refer overflow jobs.

5
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.520
With the clients or employers your positioning statement names.

6
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:37.960
With connectors, such as event organisers and association leaders.

7
00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.150
And with mentors, whose path you would like to follow.

8
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:54.390
The most common mistake is a stranger getting a message like: Hello ma, please I need a job in your company. It asks for a big favour before any relationship exists.

9
00:00:55.640 --> 00:01:08.500
For example, Kemi wants to move into customer experience at a fintech company. She follows a manager there and reads her posts for two weeks, then leaves one thoughtful comment from her own experience.

10
00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:20.730
Her note names the post she enjoyed, her six years in bank customer service, and asks only to connect. A month later she asks for a 15-minute chat, and the manager says yes.

11
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:35.000
Not every friendly contact is genuine. Be careful with anyone who quickly moves to money or asks for an upfront processing fee for a job. Real employers do not charge applicants to be hired.

12
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:44.740
Never let anyone push you to meet alone at a private address. Meet in public or by video call first, and tell someone where you are going.

13
00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:56.550
And on your side, never add new contacts to your sales group or broadcast list without asking. After two polite follow-ups with no reply, move on graciously.

14
00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:12.330
Now your proof. Open your Brand before album from module one, take matching after screenshots, and place each pair side by side. Remember Amaka, the Lagos cake baker. Before, her WhatsApp scored 1 out of 5.

15
00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:22.580
After: a clear name and photo, a useful About line, a catalogue of 10 cakes with starting prices, plus greeting, away and quick replies.

16
00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:33.130
After 6 weeks, her enquiry log showed 9 new customers. Her capstone page shows both screenshots, a list of 8 changes, and that real result.

17
00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:45.340
Your work portfolio needs three to six strong, recent pieces. For each, say what the client needed, what you did and the result. Then prepare a short spoken pitch.

18
00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:52.070
Halima says: I help small shop owners in Kano see their real profit each month.

19
00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:59.490
Last quarter, one pharmacy client found it was losing money on two product lines and dropped them.

20
00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:04.730
If you run a shop, I can do a free 20-minute review of your records.

21
00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:11.290
Aim for about 75 words. Only claim results you directly caused or contributed to.

22
00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:26.150
A brand stays strong with a simple routine and a plan with dates. For example, Blessing, the Benin City hairstylist, starts from her log: about 12 new WhatsApp enquiries a month, 3 from Instagram.

23
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:34.690
In days 1 to 30 she fixes gaps. Her target is 5 written client reviews, with permission, by day 30.

24
00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:43.300
In days 31 to 60 she keeps posting and connects with 15 salon owners or managers on LinkedIn.

25
00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:53.940
By day 90 she aims for 18 enquiries a month, at least 6 from Instagram. Become famous is not a target. A number you can count is.

26
00:03:55.190 --> 00:04:11.360
Your practice. Start five relationships with comments and personal notes. Build your before-and-after document. Choose three to six portfolio items with permissions saved. Record your 30-second pitch, and write your 90-day plan with dated targets.

27
00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.860
Now continue with the lessons below.
